<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" style="text-align: justify;">
                <h2><b>Unlocking the Full Potential of Dynamics 365 with Customization</b></h2>
                <p>
                    iFOX helps organizations tailor Dynamics 365 to their business processes, users, and data. Our Dynamics 365 customization services begin with understanding requirements, often alongside <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/CRM%20Consulting">CRM consulting</a>, and then apply maintainable configuration and targeted development so the platform supports practical day-to-day work. Configuration uses the platform's standard settings, such as forms, views, fields, security roles, and business rules. Customization extends that foundation when standard configuration is not enough, using solutions such as custom workflows, plugins, scripts, or integrations.
                </p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Custom Workflows and Business Rules: Design custom workflows and business rules that align with your organization’s processes, helping automate repeatable work and reduce manual tasks.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Custom Entities and Fields: Create custom entities and fields to capture unique business data that Dynamics 365 does not address out of the box, ensuring relevant information is tracked in Dataverse.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Form and View Customization: Modify forms and views to enhance user experience and provide staff with only the data they need, improving efficiency and reducing clutter.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Integration with Third-Party Applications: Customize Dynamics 365 to integrate with third-party software, supporting connected processes and consistent data exchange where your business requires it.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Role-Based Personalization: Customize the interface and functionality based on user roles to ensure that every team member has access to the tools they need for maximum productivity.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />
                <h2><b>Best Practices for Customizing Dynamics 365 to Fit Your Business Needs?</b></h2>
                <p>
                    iFOX follows a structured approach to Dynamics 365 customization: define requirements, review the standard configuration, design the solution, develop and test changes, and prepare documentation for handover. When customization is part of a broader <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Implementation">Dynamics 365 implementation</a>, the same approach helps coordinate configuration, testing, and adoption. Typical deliverables include configured components, custom workflows or extensions, tested solution changes, and handover documentation. This process helps improve process consistency, user adoption, and maintainability while keeping deliverables easier to review and extend as requirements evolve.
                    </p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Clear Requirements Definition: Start by defining business requirements, affected users, data, and acceptance criteria before development so the solution aligns with operational objectives.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Maintainability Focus: When customizing, prioritize solutions that are easy to maintain and update over time, avoiding overly complex or fragile customizations.
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Version Control: Implement version control for your custom solutions, ensuring you can track changes and revert if necessary without disrupting system performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Testing and Quality Assurance: Thoroughly test customizations in a non-production environment to prevent issues and ensure that all changes work as intended before going live.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Documentation and Handover: Document the configured components, custom workflows, solution changes, and operational considerations so teams can manage and update the customization with greater confidence.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman analyzing-checking-finance-graphs-office.webp" class="img-fluid text-center m-3" alt="Woman analyzing financial graphs in an office" /></div>
